    <Set guid="7E8D3DE5-C70E-4A19-A570-11F920CE6293" name="Challenges">
      <Description>Defintion: A challenge is a recurrent condition, constraint, or source of difficulty that systematically impedes the achievement of an intended objective or the effective functioning of a process, independent of any specific solution or intervention. It denotes an underlying problem situation that requires deliberate mitigation or design-oriented response rather than an incidental or transient obstacle. (Hevner, 2004) Inclusion criteria: •The phenomenon is described as a persistent or structural impediment rather than a one-off incident. •The impediment affects goal attainment, coordination, interpretation, or execution at a systemic level. •The description is solution-agnostic and focuses on the problem condition itself. •The challenge recurs across cases, contexts, organizations, or domains, or is argued to be inherent to the setting. •The challenge is analytically separable from implementation choices, tools, or specific projects. Exclusion criteria: •Descriptions limited to specific solutions, technologies, methods, or design artefacts without abstraction to an underlying problem. •Incidental errors, temporary disruptions, or context-specific failures lacking broader relevance. •Normative recommendations or best practices that do not explicate an underlying impediment. •Outcomes, impacts, or consequences without an explicit articulation of the causal problem condition. •Purely organizational preferences or political positions unless framed as systematic constraints.</Description>
      <MemberCode guid="1C66EB48-15AB-4BFA-9930-837693063DB2"></MemberCode>
      <MemberCode guid="237236D6-4DAC-4177-8619-BB73BF4B44EF"></MemberCode>
      <MemberCode guid="47ED5F0D-D237-4B26-AC21-D62915A558EC"></MemberCode>
      <MemberCode guid="5FFCDFCE-2AC4-42C0-A759-18B3CC6FD769"></MemberCode>
      <MemberCode guid="83FDB7EC-524E-46C3-AC23-D058F71D3647"></MemberCode>
